The clerk has my passport and my registration.
He is registering the SIM card now.
He has the card and a piece of paper for me.
"Here is your new number, Frau Flores," the clerk says.
I look at the piece of paper.
I put the SIM card into my mobile phone.
I read the number aloud.
"My number is zero one seven six...", I say.
"... one two three four, five six seven eight."
The clerk nods.
"Yes, that is right," he says.
I finally have a telephone number in Germany!
I immediately write a message to Jonas.
"Hello Jonas, it is me, Maya."
"This is my new number for work."
Jonas replies very quickly.
"Super, thank you!" he writes.
The card costs fifteen euros and I pay.
"Thank you very much for your help and goodbye," I say to the clerk.
